286
00:12:38,528 --> 00:12:42,048
Double riding a bicycle like that is a serious breach of the law.

287
00:12:42,048 --> 00:12:44,448
I'm going to contact your parents and your school.

288
00:12:44,448 --> 00:12:46,848
Kiyotaro, how could you do this to me?

289
00:12:47,488 --> 00:12:49,168
She was riding on that loner's bike.

290
00:12:49,168 --> 00:12:50,128
Did he force her?

291
00:12:51,008 --> 00:12:53,728
I had to quit my modeling career.

292
00:12:54,928 --> 00:12:57,328
I'd never allow myself to do something like that.

293
00:12:59,328 --> 00:13:03,968
Hey, Ichikawa, do you prefer the standard coffee flavor poppiko

294
00:13:03,968 --> 00:13:05,408
or the white sour ones more?

295
00:13:06,128 --> 00:13:07,648
Oh, the coffee ones?

296
00:13:08,288 --> 00:13:08,688
Ooh.

297
00:13:09,888 --> 00:13:11,728
Afraid of a little bit of change, aren't you?

298
00:13:11,728 --> 00:13:12,608
Huh?

299
00:13:14,448 --> 00:13:17,088
The light's green.

300
00:13:20,928 --> 00:13:21,168
Right.

301
00:13:23,008 --> 00:13:24,288
I've always been sick.

302
00:13:29,648 --> 00:13:31,408
There's just something wrong with my head.

303
00:13:35,008 --> 00:13:36,768
Thanks, bet I felt heavy.

304
00:13:36,768 --> 00:13:38,208
No, not a bit.

305
00:13:39,008 --> 00:13:40,848
Guess I've no choice but to give you this.

306
00:13:40,848 --> 00:13:42,128
Huh?

307
00:13:42,128 --> 00:13:43,488
Wait, what?

308
00:13:43,488 --> 00:13:43,808
Huh?

309
00:13:44,528 --> 00:13:45,968
Don't act that surprised.

310
00:13:49,168 --> 00:13:49,408
Okay.

311
00:13:50,528 --> 00:13:50,848
Here.

312
00:13:50,848 --> 00:13:51,888
Uh.

313
00:13:58,848 --> 00:14:00,528
Was that the right way to react?

314
00:14:01,968 --> 00:14:02,528
See ya.

315
00:14:02,528 --> 00:14:06,128
Maybe I should raise my hand higher?

316
00:14:10,688 --> 00:14:12,288
All right, class, listen up.

317
00:14:13,008 --> 00:14:17,488
Apparently someone threw away some sort of snack food wrapper in the library trash.

318
00:14:18,448 --> 00:14:21,888
Now, all of you know it's against the rules to bring in snacks.

319
00:14:21,888 --> 00:14:25,808
Playing with your eraser?

320
00:14:25,808 --> 00:14:27,248
What are you, a third grader?

321
00:14:28,928 --> 00:14:33,408
If we're having this talk now after the whole Puruche incident, then I bet...

322
00:14:33,408 --> 00:14:34,848
Yamada?

323
00:14:34,848 --> 00:14:35,408
Huh?

324
00:14:35,408 --> 00:14:37,648
Any idea who it could be?

325
00:14:37,648 --> 00:14:39,568
You should have been ready for this!

326
00:14:40,368 --> 00:14:43,168
I never threw anything in the trash, so it couldn't be me.

327
00:14:49,248 --> 00:14:50,368
Yamada?

328
00:14:50,368 --> 00:14:52,768
I want you in the teacher's office after class.

329
00:14:52,768 --> 00:14:53,488
What?

330
00:14:53,488 --> 00:14:54,928
Such a dumbass.

331
00:14:54,928 --> 00:14:55,808
I am?

332
00:14:55,808 --> 00:14:56,848
But why?

333
00:14:56,848 --> 00:14:58,608
An idiot through and through, huh?

334
00:14:59,968 --> 00:15:01,248
This could be a problem, though.

335
00:15:05,088 --> 00:15:08,448
Our teacher was busy, so Yamada's off the hook until next week.

336
00:15:09,088 --> 00:15:14,848
But if she can't bring snacks in anymore, that means she won't drop by the library.

337
00:15:16,688 --> 00:15:17,968
I'm exhausted.

338
00:15:17,968 --> 00:15:21,488
I had to work five days in a row, and now I'm here babysitting.

339
00:15:21,488 --> 00:15:23,568
You're the one who dragged me out to this place.

340
00:15:24,688 --> 00:15:26,048
Thanks for coming with me.

341
00:15:26,608 --> 00:15:27,488
Darling brother.

342
00:15:27,488 --> 00:15:28,288
Don't give me that!

343
00:15:30,288 --> 00:15:32,928
I wanted to use this time to think up a plan, too.

344
00:15:34,448 --> 00:15:38,128
If anyone from my class caught me here with this idiot, I'd just die.

345
00:15:39,408 --> 00:15:39,648
Wait.

346
00:15:40,368 --> 00:15:41,488
Stop thinking like that.

347
00:15:42,208 --> 00:15:43,168
Every time you do,

348
00:15:45,488 --> 00:15:47,008
it always comes true!

349
00:15:47,008 --> 00:15:48,448
Okay, Abel, you're right.

350
00:15:51,568 --> 00:15:52,448
What's wrong?

351
00:15:52,448 --> 00:15:53,168
Enough of you!

352
00:15:53,888 --> 00:15:55,968
Gotta admit, I was surprised.

353
00:15:56,928 --> 00:15:59,088
Didn't think no one would hit on us.

354
00:15:59,088 --> 00:16:00,208
I'm sorry.

355
00:16:00,208 --> 00:16:03,088
Does anyone ever actually hit on you when you're out in public?

356
00:16:03,728 --> 00:16:05,568
I kind of want to know the answer to that.

357
00:16:05,568 --> 00:16:08,848
Well, someone did come up and talk to anyone.

358
00:16:09,408 --> 00:16:13,088
But it doesn't count, because it was just some random relative of mine.

359
00:16:13,088 --> 00:16:14,928
I can't hear a word she's saying.

360
00:16:14,928 --> 00:16:16,688
Chill out with the seasoning pack!

361
00:16:16,688 --> 00:16:17,648
Hey, little brother.

362
00:16:17,648 --> 00:16:20,288
You sure that's enough?

363
00:16:20,288 --> 00:16:22,928
You look like some girl on a diet with just a salad.

364
00:16:24,368 --> 00:16:26,288
Shut your mouth, you idiot!

365
00:16:26,288 --> 00:16:28,208
Here, a present from your big sis.

366
00:16:28,768 --> 00:16:30,608
You're still a growing boy, after all.

367
00:16:30,608 --> 00:16:31,248
Huh?

368
00:16:32,448 --> 00:16:32,768
Fine.

369
00:16:33,648 --> 00:16:35,648
I'm gonna go buy something else to eat.

370
00:16:38,448 --> 00:16:39,888
Welcome, how can I help you?

371
00:16:41,008 --> 00:16:42,368
I needed to get out of there.

372
00:16:43,088 --> 00:16:45,728
Why do my worst nightmares always come true?

373
00:16:45,728 --> 00:16:46,528
Hey!

374
00:16:49,328 --> 00:16:49,728
Wow.

375
00:16:49,728 --> 00:16:51,008
Watch it.

376
00:16:52,608 --> 00:16:53,968
Is she trying to pick a fight?

377
00:16:53,968 --> 00:16:56,528
Was that your sister sitting with you?

378
00:16:56,528 --> 00:16:57,568
She's super cute.

379
00:16:57,568 --> 00:17:00,528
She's always trying to do everything for me.

380
00:17:00,528 --> 00:17:01,088
It's dumb.

381
00:17:01,088 --> 00:17:02,448
Oh, really?

382
00:17:02,448 --> 00:17:03,968
I wish she could be my friend.

383
00:17:03,968 --> 00:17:04,528
Hmm?

384
00:17:04,528 --> 00:17:07,008
So she could do everything for you?

385
00:17:07,008 --> 00:17:07,968
Sheesh.

386
00:17:07,968 --> 00:17:09,488
I'm kind of jealous.

387
00:17:09,488 --> 00:17:10,848
I'm an only child, you see.

388
00:17:11,568 --> 00:17:12,928
Yeah, I could have guessed.

389
00:17:14,128 --> 00:17:15,328
Everyone says that.

390
00:17:19,248 --> 00:17:20,208
What are you gonna get?

391
00:17:20,208 --> 00:17:21,888
Seasoned chicken.

392
00:17:21,888 --> 00:17:23,568
Oh, copying me.

393
00:17:24,368 --> 00:17:25,408
Busted dude!

394
00:17:26,768 --> 00:17:29,248
She looks so grown up out of her uniform.

395
00:17:29,248 --> 00:17:32,208
Maybe I'll go ahead and get something as well.

396
00:17:32,208 --> 00:17:34,128
Ooh, I want some soft serve.

397
00:17:36,048 --> 00:17:38,528
Oh shoot, my wallet is upstairs.

398
00:17:38,528 --> 00:17:39,888
Were you not getting something?

399
00:17:40,848 --> 00:17:43,728
I needed to pee.

400
00:17:44,448 --> 00:17:46,208
The bathrooms are all upstairs though.

401
00:17:47,728 --> 00:17:48,928
Oh, whoopsie!

402
00:17:48,928 --> 00:17:50,368
Imagine that!

403
00:17:52,768 --> 00:17:53,648
See ya!

404
00:17:53,648 --> 00:17:54,608
Thanks for waiting.

405
00:17:55,488 --> 00:17:55,968
Sheesh.

406
00:17:57,648 --> 00:18:00,448
Wait, did she come down just to talk to me?

407
00:18:00,448 --> 00:18:01,408
Are you ready to order?

408
00:18:02,208 --> 00:18:04,608
Uh, um, the seasoned chicken and...

409
00:18:06,128 --> 00:18:07,888
No, why would she?

410
00:18:07,888 --> 00:18:10,448
I bet she really just didn't know where the bathrooms were.

411
00:18:11,008 --> 00:18:12,208
Will that be all then?

412
00:18:12,208 --> 00:18:14,288
No, um, let me get...

413
00:18:15,808 --> 00:18:17,248
What did I buy this for?

414
00:18:18,048 --> 00:18:19,808
It's not like I could give it to her.

415
00:18:19,808 --> 00:18:24,288
Uh, uh, uh, this is...

416
00:18:25,568 --> 00:18:27,648
Well, copied me again, huh?

417
00:18:29,648 --> 00:18:30,528
No, I gotta...

418
00:18:33,408 --> 00:18:35,248
She smells so nice.

419
00:18:39,408 --> 00:18:41,008
Yamada's still not here?

420
00:18:41,888 --> 00:18:43,568
I bet she completely forgot.

421
00:18:43,568 --> 00:18:43,888
Hey!

422
00:18:46,528 --> 00:18:47,328
Seriously?

423
00:18:47,328 --> 00:18:48,688
Quit popping up like that!

424
00:18:49,648 --> 00:18:50,688
What's the matter?

425
00:18:50,688 --> 00:18:52,608
You need to talk to a teacher or something?

426
00:18:52,608 --> 00:18:55,488
N-no, I was just passing by here is all.

427
00:18:56,048 --> 00:18:57,408
Then come in with me.

428
00:18:58,128 --> 00:18:58,928
Why is that?

429
00:18:58,928 --> 00:18:59,728
Because I'm scared.

430
00:19:00,848 --> 00:19:02,288
That's got nothing to do with me.

431
00:19:03,168 --> 00:19:03,808
Are you sure?

432
00:19:05,088 --> 00:19:05,888
Okay, maybe not...

433
00:19:06,608 --> 00:19:07,008
nothing.

434
00:19:10,528 --> 00:19:11,488
Ichikawa?

435
00:19:11,488 --> 00:19:12,528
Why are you here?

436
00:19:12,528 --> 00:19:14,688
Um, just here to observe, sir.

437
00:19:14,688 --> 00:19:16,688
And to keep things totally transparent.

438
00:19:16,688 --> 00:19:18,448
Oh, I see then.

439
00:19:18,448 --> 00:19:20,928
To make sure I don't pull any dirty tricks on you, huh?

440
00:19:20,928 --> 00:19:23,648
Huh, I guess you can be smart sometimes.

441
00:19:23,648 --> 00:19:28,688
You know very well that snacks aren't allowed anywhere on the premises.

442
00:19:28,688 --> 00:19:30,688
Who brought any snacks into school?

443
00:19:30,688 --> 00:19:31,568
You think it was me?

444
00:19:32,128 --> 00:19:33,248
Listen here.

445
00:19:33,248 --> 00:19:36,208
I already know about the incident that happened in the science lab.

446
00:19:36,208 --> 00:19:39,888
Sir, Miss Yamada never admitted to bringing in any snacks.

447
00:19:40,768 --> 00:19:41,728
What are you saying?

448
00:19:41,728 --> 00:19:47,088
Sir, you're trying to find out who it was that threw away that snack wrapper back in the library.

449
00:19:47,088 --> 00:19:49,728
And you're asking whether or not it was Yamada who did it.

450
00:19:50,368 --> 00:19:53,328
All Miss Yamada did say was that she did not do it.

451
00:19:53,328 --> 00:19:58,288
Oh, she only answered that way because she is bringing in some snacks.

452
00:19:58,288 --> 00:20:02,448
Normally you wouldn't word it like that, just say so if you weren't bringing any in.

453
00:20:02,448 --> 00:20:04,528
Yes, normally you wouldn't.

454
00:20:05,088 --> 00:20:05,328
What?

455
00:20:06,608 --> 00:20:09,088
Normally someone would know what you were truly asking.

456
00:20:09,728 --> 00:20:12,208
But some people just answer the question that's asked.

457
00:20:13,248 --> 00:20:16,288
Sir, which group do you think Miss Yamada falls in?

458
00:20:17,968 --> 00:20:19,168
Maybe, but...

459
00:20:19,168 --> 00:20:22,768
Miss Yamada didn't throw the wrapper away and never said she brought snacks in.

460
00:20:23,328 --> 00:20:24,048
And that's that.

461
00:20:25,008 --> 00:20:25,648
BAM!

462
00:20:25,648 --> 00:20:26,048
Got him.

463
00:20:26,848 --> 00:20:28,128
That's all I came to say.

464
00:20:28,128 --> 00:20:28,368
Bye.

465
00:20:30,288 --> 00:20:30,688
Ichikawa.

466
00:20:32,288 --> 00:20:33,168
No good, huh?

467
00:20:35,328 --> 00:20:36,048
Impressive!

468
00:20:36,048 --> 00:20:38,048
Never seen you talk this much before.

469
00:20:38,608 --> 00:20:39,248
I'm happy.

470
00:20:39,248 --> 00:20:40,288
Glad to see it.

471
00:20:40,288 --> 00:20:41,328
Give me a break!

472
00:20:41,328 --> 00:20:47,968
Not sure I really liked your logic there, but thanks.

473
00:20:49,248 --> 00:20:51,248
It was just a bit of sophism.

474
00:20:53,408 --> 00:20:54,688
Let me give you some candy.

475
00:20:55,808 --> 00:20:56,688
Which one do you want?

476
00:20:57,648 --> 00:20:59,408
Only one of those is even candy!

477
00:20:59,408 --> 00:21:11,328
You're such a dorky little kid.

478
00:21:11,328 --> 00:21:11,968
What?

479
00:21:11,968 --> 00:21:15,088
Oh, we should...

480
00:21:17,808 --> 00:21:18,768
Talk like friends.

481
00:21:24,768 --> 00:21:29,008
N-not like how we talk is a big deal or anything.

482
00:21:29,008 --> 00:21:31,888
Happy dinner.

483
00:21:34,128 --> 00:21:34,848
Wow.

484
00:21:34,848 --> 00:21:35,568
What happened?

485
00:21:35,568 --> 00:21:36,928
You didn't get a little cold, but nothing!

486
00:21:36,928 --> 00:21:37,648
This is a condom project.

